From be42f68bfcbfbc16b460da118d3093b6ed36a1a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:32:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 155/156] wifi: mt6797: transmit the supplicant's control-port
 EAPOL frames on TC4

Phase C2 lets the standard supplicant complete the four-way handshake.
Its replies reach the driver from mac80211's control-port path as
non-QoS To-DS data frames with the LLC/SNAP EAPOL type, flagged as port
control protocol.

Admit exactly that shape to the target from this station, at most two
per lifetime, only after an accepted association and before the
deauthentication, into the one existing queue. The pinned gen3 driver
sends every 802.1X frame as a security-frame command on TC4 with the
long descriptor, header format non-802.11 with the Ethernet II flag and
a PID with TX status to the MCU; encode that descriptor beside the
management one, prepare it through the same ledger, and send it through
the same PIO owner. At submission the 802.11 frame becomes an Ethernet
II frame in a driver buffer (destination from address 3, source from
address 2, type from the SNAP header); the mac80211 skb is untouched
and remains the frame whose status is reported.

The queue stays one queue: the dequeue step takes the first frame that
is neither the driver-built deauthentication during its hold nor a data
frame before the station activation, so a reply queued behind the held
deauthentication is sent while the deauthentication keeps its place.
Pages, PID, deadlines, the single in-flight frame and the TX-done path
are unchanged.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
